lunduke-edit (0.9-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Insert toggles overwrite only with no modifiers, including the keypad,
    and Shift+Insert / Ctrl+Insert reach the text view. The status mode
    follows the text view. Paste, middle-click, and drag-and-drop reject
    an oversized clipboard from the selection length before the text is
    copied, and the checked text is what gets inserted.
  * A hard-linked save stages the new bytes before copying them into the
    existing inode, and a short write says the file may be damaged. A
    directory flush failure after a successful rename is not a failed
    save. New files use 0666 masked by umask, and the temporary file stays
    private until it replaces the destination.
  * Saving uses openat, O_NOFOLLOW, and renameat. Extended attributes,
    including ACLs and the security context, are copied onto the new
    inode. A clean buffer is not rewritten. A writable file in a
    directory that is not writable, and a very long name, still save.
  * Mixed newline styles are written back as loaded. Pasted carriage
    returns are not expanded again. Search Selection Only and Extend
    Selection pins clear when the buffer is replaced. Fifos are rejected
    without a blocking open.
  * A file larger than 32 MiB still asks before opening. A file larger
    than 64 MiB is refused, with no unlimited read on the UI thread.
  * Opens that arrive during a dialog or a clipboard wait are queued.
    Find yields while skipping non-word matches. Cancelling Replace All
    undoes the partial edit. Closing Find clears highlights. Encoding
    radios follow the document; the next Open has its own control. A path
    that is already open is shown instead of loaded again, and a file
    that changed on disk is not replaced without asking. Wrap stays off
    while a line is still too long. Recent paths cannot contain a newline,
    and a failed lock does not rewrite the recent list. Print caches one
    layout per page, measures tab stops from the print context, and does
    not split a line into a second layout.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 14:30:00 -0500

lunduke-edit (0.9-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Saving through a symlink updates the target and leaves the link in
    place. A broken symlink is not replaced. A file with other hard links
    is updated in place. The previous owner is restored when the process
    is allowed to, and the new bytes and directory entry are flushed.
  * Opening a file in an already-running instance reuses a window only
    when that window is focused and still empty. Other documents stay
    put, and a file that cannot be read does not leave an extra window.
    A closed window is freed. Cancelling the close of an unsaved document
    keeps the window.
  * The status-bar size is the number of bytes a save would write, cached
    from edits. Cursor motion no longer walks a multi-megabyte line.
  * Files larger than 32 MiB ask before opening. A paste larger than
    32 MiB is refused. A read continues to end of file, including files
    that report a size of zero. Only local files can be opened or saved.
  * Find All and Replace All run in chunks so Cancel stays responsive,
    stop after a large number of hits, and ask before storing a huge undo
    record. Search Backwards is honored. The match count is its own
    status label and clears when the text changes.
  * Recent files are one list shared by every window. A new document is
    UTF-8. The Text menu charset applies to the next Open and is inherited
    by new windows, along with font, wrap, and tab width. Word wrap
    defaults to off, and a very long line turns wrap off in that window.
  * CRLF and CR line endings are kept and written back on save. Printing
    paginates long documents and uses the editor's tab stops.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 00:42:00 -0500

